# Review ownership. A pull request touching a path below automatically requests a review from its
# owner.
#
# GitHub applies exactly one rule per file, and it is the LAST pattern that matches — not the most
# specific one. The catch-all is therefore written first and the narrower paths after it; reversing
# the order would leave `*` overriding everything below it.

# The project itself: application code, Gradle build scripts and documentation.
*           @gdinn

# CI workflows and repository configuration, including this file. These paths decide how everything
# above is built, signed and published, so ownership of them is ownership of the release path.
/.github/   @gdinn
